Project Implementation Rules
	1.	Always Review Existing Implementation Before Coding
Before writing any new code, always examine the existing implementation. Specifically check:
	•	Naming conventions for functions and variables
	•	How comments are structured
	•	How similar functionality is implemented
Your new work should follow the patterns already established in the codebase.
	2.	When Multiple Implementation Options Exist, Follow Established Practice
If there are multiple ways to implement a feature, first find similar functionality in the existing code. Study how it was done and then implement your feature using the same approach and style.
	3.	Adhere to All Skills Guidelines and Agent.md Rules
All contributions must comply with the guidelines outlined in Skills as well as the Agent.md documentation.
	4.	Always Be Conscious of the Architecture
Keep the system architecture in mind when implementing features. Understand the architectural decisions and details captured in the design documents, and ensure your implementation aligns with them.
